WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.620
In 1844, in Persia, a man called the Báb
declared that he was a messenger of God.

2
00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:08.970
He said a greater one would follow.

3
00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:11.670
In 1850 he was executed.

4
00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:17.130
In 1863, in a garden in Baghdad,
Bahá'u'lláh declared that he was the one the

5
00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:18.730
Báb foretold.

6
00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:21.870
So how can one faith
honour Moses, the Buddha,

7
00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:26.280
Jesus and Muhammad, yet say a
new messenger came after them?

8
00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:31.140
In this mission, you'll meet the Bahá'í
image of a mirror reflecting the sun.

9
00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:35.680
Then you'll see why Bahá'ís call
heaven and hell states, not places.

10
00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:40.150
Your mission: explain how one faith
can honour earlier messengers,

11
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:42.190
yet say a new one came after them.
